  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper implements quantum amplitude estimation for European call option pricing on a tokenized Bitcoin asset using Qiskit Aer simulation with ~9 qubits, ~150 circuit depth, and 8,192 shots. Across 3–6 price qubits (8–64 bins), discretization error decreases exactly 2× per qubit doubling (from $49,616 to $6,202), empirically validating the expected scaling, but the practical estimate at 5 qubits ($14,288 ± $12,404) is far less precise than classical Monte Carlo.",
